Q: How do I prepend file to beginning? A: <p>I turned the answer above from @ashastral into a self contained function. I'm only just beginning to understand what it's doing...</p>
<pre><code>//
// Prepends a string to a file
//
// @param string $name    The filename to prepend to
// @param string $prepend The str to prepend
//
//
function file_prepend ($name, $prepend)
{
    $buf1 = $prepend; // This gets prepended
    $file = $name;    // The file to which $cache_new
                      // gets prepended

    $fp        = fopen($file, 'r+');
    $len       = strlen($buf1);
    $final_len = filesize($file) + $len;
    $buf2      = fread($fp, $len);

    rewind($fp);
    $i = 1;

    while (ftell($fp) &lt; $final_len) {
        fwrite($fp, $buf1);
        $buf1 = $buf2;
        $buf2 = fread($fp, $len);
        fseek($fp, $i * $len);
        $i++;
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: The auto-completion for await changes the method&#39;s signature - how do I prevent that? A: <p>I found a temporary solution that can perfectly meet your needs. Just import an 'await' snippet and then it will only insert 'await' without changing any code:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-8&quot; ?&gt;
&lt;CodeSnippets  xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/VisualStudio/2005/CodeSnippet&quot;&gt;
    &lt;CodeSnippet Format=&quot;1.0.0&quot;&gt;
        &lt;Header&gt;
            &lt;Title&gt;await&lt;/Title&gt;
            &lt;Shortcut&gt;await&lt;/Shortcut&gt;
            &lt;Description&gt;Code snippet for 'await' keyword&lt;/Description&gt;
            &lt;Author&gt;Shingo&lt;/Author&gt;
            &lt;SnippetTypes&gt;
                &lt;SnippetType&gt;Expansion&lt;/SnippetType&gt;
            &lt;/SnippetTypes&gt;
        &lt;/Header&gt;
        &lt;Snippet&gt;
            &lt;Code Language=&quot;csharp&quot;&gt;&lt;![CDATA[await $end$]]&gt;
            &lt;/Code&gt;
        &lt;/Snippet&gt;
    &lt;/CodeSnippet&gt;
&lt;/CodeSnippets&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: I want to preview HTML form data in pop window before submit. How to do that using JavaScript? A: <p>There is many ways to achieve that, but you can start with HTML native <strong>Dialog</strong> element.</p>
<p>Here is a basic example:
<a href="https://codepen.io/The-Tirius/pen/YPWrGEL" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codepen.io/The-Tirius/pen/YPWrGEL</a></p>
<p><strong>HTML</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;form&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;
        Name
        &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;name&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;

    &lt;label&gt;
        Surname
        &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;surname&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;

    &lt;button class=&quot;btn-confirm&quot;&gt;Confirm data&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;

&lt;dialog&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Please check your data before submit&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;ul class=&quot;form-data&quot;&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;button class=&quot;btn-close&quot;&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;button class=&quot;btn-submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/dialog&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>CSS</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>label, input {
    display: block;
}

label {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

dialog {
    border: none;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 2rem;
    max-width: 400px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>JS</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const elForm = document.querySelector('form');
const elBtnConfirm = elForm.querySelector('.btn-confirm');

const elDialog = document.querySelector('dialog');
const elDialogFormData = elDialog.querySelector('.form-data');
const elBtnClose = elDialog.querySelector('.btn-close');
const elBtnSubmit = elDialog.querySelector('.btn-submit');

elBtnConfirm.addEventListener('click', e =&gt; {
    e.preventDefault();

    const formData = new FormData(elForm);
    let html = '';

    for (let [name, value] of formData) {
        html += `&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;${name}&lt;/b&gt;: ${value || '...'}&lt;/li&gt;`;
    }

    elDialogFormData.innerHTML = html;
    elDialog.showModal();
});

elBtnClose.addEventListener('click', e =&gt; {
    elDialog.close();
});

elBtnSubmit.addEventListener('click', e =&gt; {
    elDialog.close();
    alert('Form submitted...');
});
</code></pre>
